Cador: implement the ActiveX surface required by SCHME+ A1 tests

== Context ==

SCHME+ now has an A1 test batch for its thin ActiveX adapters. Running it with
ALFE/Cador exposes four missing parts of the mock AutoCAD object model. The
same tests are intended to run without skips on AutoCAD and BricsCAD.

    cd ../schme
    make test-cad-activex-alfe CAD=clautolisp

The entry point is `tests/test-cad-activex-adaptateurs.lsp`.

== Missing surface ==

1. `AutoCAD.Documents.Add`, followed by `Document.SaveAs` and `Close`, for
   `util_creer_dwg_vide`.

       VLA-OBJECT AutoCAD.Documents has no method named ADD.

2. Read/write `AutoCAD.Layer.Color` (and the layer operations used beside it:
   `Layers.Add`, `Document.ActiveLayer`, entity `Layer`, `Layer.Delete`) for
   `util_cree_calque`, selection and entity moves.

       VLA-OBJECT AutoCAD.Layer has no property named COLOR.

3. Attributed block support after the already-working `Blocks.Add`:
   `Block.AddAttribute`, `ModelSpace.InsertBlock`,
   `BlockReference.HasAttributes/GetAttributes`, attribute
   `TagString/TextString`, rotation and deletion.

4. `Document.Linetypes`, `Linetypes.Load`, `ModelSpace.AddLine` and entity
   `Linetype`, so a small `.lin` fixture can be loaded and applied.

`vlax-method-applicable-p` and `vlax-property-available-p` correctly report
the currently missing capabilities. SCHME+ uses these predicates to mark the
four scenarios SKIP under Cador until this issue is implemented.

== Acceptance ==

- Implement the object graph and mutations above against Cador's in-memory
  drawing/document model.
- Add focused Cador tests for every new method/property.
- Run the SCHME+ command above: the four A1 scenarios must execute their full
  assertions, with no `SKIP [adaptateurs-activex-a1]` line.
- Preserve the created/modified entities in `entget`/table state so the A1
  assertions observe the same data through DXF and ActiveX.
